From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Promote unselected post-cost Local feature ancestors.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Windows10 v11/v12, x64 and i686: an immediate post-CostFinalize
SetFeatureState(Local) promotes the entire measured unselected ancestor
chain. Both GetFeatureState request and published state become Local;
FP and non-FP siblings stay Absent in ADDLOCAL and level modes.
Native measurement bundles: v11 510/0, v12 546/0, both architectures, exit0.

Update ancestor requests, actions and component states directly, without
recursive SetFeatureState calls on parents. Retain B's measured propagation
from the explicitly set feature. Stop at the first selected ancestor or
disabled Level-0 ancestor, and bound traversal by the feature count. These boundaries,
maintenance and post-cost non-Local requests remain unmeasured.

v2 (2026-11-05): context-only refresh for B v2 fresh-only local_after_cost.
No ancestor logic or measured expectations changed.

Apply after A, A2 and B; do not combine with the separate test-only artifact.
The engine hunk also composes with the diagnostic trace patch. Original code,
public API observations only. Outside series pending review and validation.

diff --git a/dlls/msi/install.c b/dlls/msi/install.c
--- a/dlls/msi/install.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/install.c
@@ -934,5 +934,23 @@
     feature->ActionRequest = iState;
     local_after_cost = iState == INSTALLSTATE_LOCAL && msi_get_property_int( package->db, L"CostingComplete", 0 ) && !msi_get_property_int( package->db, L"Installed", 0 );
-    if (local_after_cost) feature->Action = iState;
+    if (local_after_cost)
+    {
+        MSIFEATURE *parent = feature;
+        unsigned int remaining = list_count( &package->features );
+
+        feature->Action = iState;
+        /* Bound the walk even for malformed Feature_Parent cycles. Calling
+         * SetFeatureState on a parent would also select its other children. */
+        while (parent->Feature_Parent && remaining--)
+        {
+            parent = msi_get_loaded_feature( package, parent->Feature_Parent );
+            if (!parent || parent->Level <= 0) break;
+            if (parent->ActionRequest != INSTALLSTATE_UNKNOWN &&
+                parent->ActionRequest != INSTALLSTATE_ABSENT) break;
+
+            parent->ActionRequest = parent->Action = INSTALLSTATE_LOCAL;
+            ACTION_UpdateComponentStates( package, parent );
+        }
+    }
 
     ACTION_UpdateComponentStates( package, feature );
